SIMPLE  =                    T / conforms to FITS standard                      BITPIX  =                    8 / array data type                                NAXIS   =                    0 / number of array dimensions                     EXTEND  =                    T                                                  TELESCOP= 'HST     '                                                            INSTRUME= 'ACS     '                                                            DETECTOR= 'WFC     '                                                            FILENAME= '4bb15371j_d2i.fits'                                                  FILETYPE= 'WFC D2I FILE'       / Type of data found in data file                OBSTYPE = 'IMAGING '           / Type of observation                            DESCRIP = 'Non-polynomial 2-D look up table correction'                         USEAFTER= 'Mar 01 2002 00:00:00'                                                PEDIGREE= 'INFLIGHT 11/11/2002 11/11/2002'                                      DATE    = '2020-08-11'                                                          ROOTNAME= '4BB15371J_D2I'                                                       COMMENT Original D2IMFILE derived by V. Kozhurina-Platais February 2019         COMMENT D2IMFILE header updated by S.L. Hoffmann September 2020                 HISTORY                                                                         HISTORY After applying the best-fitting polynomial, the residuals of the        HISTORY X and Y positions between ACS/WFC observed 47Tuc in F606W filter        HISTORY and X and Y positions from the standard astrometric catalog             HISTORY as described in Kozhurina-Platais ACS-ISR-2015-6 (and improved          HISTORY by Gaia DR2 Kozhurina-Platais ACS-ISR-2018-01) have shown fine-scale    HISTORY residual structure. The complicated and correlated structure is due to  HISTORY the pixel grid distortion, imprinted onto the detector itself           HISTORY during the manufacturing process. To remove the fine-scale              HISTORY variations, a 2-D look-up table has been modeled, which is              HISTORY bi-linearly interpolated at any point in the ACS/WFC images.            HISTORY This look-up table is analogous to ACS/WFC D2I reference file           HISTORY for AstroDrizzle.                                                       HISTORY                                                                         HISTORY The correction is stored as an image extension (D2IMARR) with           HISTORY one row in X, and one row in Y. Each element in the row or column       HISTORY specifies the correction in pixels for every pixels in the column       HISTORY (or row) in science extension. For ACS/WFC, the correction is in        HISTORY the X and Y directions for each WFC CCD chip.                           HISTORY                                                                         HISTORY This 2-D look-up table has been smoothed with a Gaussian kernel         HISTORY 64x64 bin size. The astrometric errors due to the                       HISTORY irregularities of pixel-grid imprinted on the ACS/WFC detector          HISTORY have been corrected down to the ~0.01 pixel level.                      HISTORY                                                                         HISTORY File named verap_03092020_d2im.fits is renamed acs_fixed_d2im.fits.     HISTORY                                                                         HISTORY acs_fixed_d2im.fits renamed to 4bb15371j_d2i.fits on Nov 11 2020        END                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             XTENSION= 'IMAGE   '           / Image extension                                BITPIX  =                  -32 / array data type                                NAXIS   =                    2 / number of array dimensions                     NAXIS1  =                   64                                                  NAXIS2  =                   32                                                  PCOUNT  =                    0 / number of parameters                           GCOUNT  =                    1 / number of groups                               EXTNAME = 'DX      '                                                            EXTVER  =                    1                                                  ONAXIS1 =                 4096                                                  ONAXIS2 =                 2048                                                  CDELT1  =                   64                                                  CDELT2  =                   64                                                  CCDCHIP =                    2                                                  END                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             